# / ? n N: searching forward and backward, counts and repeats. 'ignorecase' is off by default.

=== / moves to the start of the next match
ref:    pattern.txt */*
quote:  Search forward for the [count]'th occurrence of {pattern} |exclusive|.
given:  |one foo two foo
keys:   /foo<CR>
expect: one |foo two foo

=== / skips a match under the cursor
ref:    pattern.txt */*
quote:  Search forward for the [count]'th occurrence of {pattern} |exclusive|.
given:  one |foo two foo
keys:   /foo<CR>
expect: one foo two |foo

=== / finds a match on a later line
ref:    pattern.txt */*
quote:  Search forward for the [count]'th occurrence of {pattern} |exclusive|.
given:
  |one
  two
  three foo
keys:   /foo<CR>
expect:
  one
  two
  three |foo

=== / with a count finds the count'th match
ref:    pattern.txt */*
quote:  Search forward for the [count]'th occurrence of {pattern} |exclusive|.
given:  |x a1 a2 a3
keys:   2/a<CR>
expect: x a1 |a2 a3

=== / with a closing slash and no offset
ref:    pattern.txt */*
quote:  /{pattern}[/]<CR>
given:  |x foo
keys:   /foo/<CR>
expect: x |foo

=== ? moves to the start of the previous match
ref:    pattern.txt *?*
quote:  Search backward for the [count]'th previous occurrence of {pattern} |exclusive|.
given:  foo one foo |two
keys:   ?foo<CR>
expect: foo one |foo two

=== ? from inside a match goes to its start
ref:    pattern.txt *?*
quote:  Search backward for the [count]'th previous occurrence of {pattern} |exclusive|.
given:  x foo|bar
keys:   ?foo<CR>
expect: x |foobar

=== ? with a count
ref:    pattern.txt *?*
quote:  Search backward for the [count]'th previous occurrence of {pattern} |exclusive|.
given:  a1 a2 a3 |x
keys:   2?a<CR>
expect: a1 |a2 a3 x

=== ? finds a match on an earlier line
ref:    pattern.txt *?*
quote:  Search backward for the [count]'th previous occurrence of {pattern} |exclusive|.
given:
  foo one
  two
  |three
keys:   ?foo<CR>
expect:
  |foo one
  two
  three

=== n repeats the last /
ref:    pattern.txt *n*
quote:  Repeat the latest "/" or "?" [count] times.
given:  |a1 a2 a3 a4
keys:   /a<CR>n
expect: a1 a2 |a3 a4

=== n with a count
ref:    pattern.txt *n*
quote:  Repeat the latest "/" or "?" [count] times.
given:  |a1 a2 a3 a4 a5
keys:   /a<CR>3n
expect: a1 a2 a3 a4 |a5

=== N repeats / in the opposite direction
ref:    pattern.txt *N*
quote:  Repeat the latest "/" or "?" [count] times in opposite direction.
given:  a1 a2 |x a3
keys:   /a<CR>N
expect: a1 |a2 x a3

=== n after ? keeps searching backward
ref:    pattern.txt *n*
quote:  Repeat the latest "/" or "?" [count] times.
given:  a1 a2 a3 |x
keys:   ?a<CR>n
expect: a1 |a2 a3 x

=== N after ? searches forward
ref:    pattern.txt *N*
quote:  Repeat the latest "/" or "?" [count] times in opposite direction.
given:  a1 a2 a3 |x
keys:   ?a<CR>?a<CR>N
expect: a1 a2 |a3 x

=== /<CR> searches again for the last pattern
ref:    pattern.txt */<CR>*
quote:  Search forward for the [count]'th occurrence of the latest used pattern |last-pattern| with latest used |{offset}|.
given:  |a1 a2 a3
keys:   /a<CR>/<CR>
expect: a1 a2 |a3

=== ?<CR> searches back for the last pattern
ref:    pattern.txt *?<CR>*
quote:  Search backward for the [count]'th occurrence of the latest used pattern |last-pattern| with latest used |{offset}|.
given:  a1 a2 a3 |x
keys:   ?a<CR>?<CR>
expect: a1 |a2 a3 x

=== / is a jump
ref:    motion.txt *jump-motions*
quote:  The following commands are "jump" commands: "'", "`", "G", "/", "?", "n", "N"
given:
  o|ne
  two foo
keys:   /foo<CR>
expect:
  one
  two |foo
jumps:  1:1

=== n is a jump
ref:    motion.txt *jump-motions*
quote:  The following commands are "jump" commands: "'", "`", "G", "/", "?", "n", "N"
given:
  |foo
  foo
  foo
keys:   /foo<CR>n
expect:
  foo
  foo
  |foo
jumps:  1:0 2:0

=== 'ignorecase' is off by default
ref:    options.txt *'ignorecase'*
quote:  'ignorecase' 'ic'	boolean	(default off)
given:  |x Foo FOO foo
keys:   /foo<CR>
expect: x Foo FOO |foo

=== \c in a search ignores case
ref:    pattern.txt */\c*
quote:  When "\c" appears anywhere in the pattern, the whole pattern is handled like 'ignorecase' is on.
given:  |x FOO foo
keys:   /foo\c<CR>
expect: x |FOO foo

=== \C in a search matches case
ref:    pattern.txt */\C*
quote:  "\"\\C\" does the opposite: Force matching case for the whole pattern."
given:  |x FOO foo
keys:   /\Cfoo<CR>
expect: x FOO |foo

=== search for a pattern that isn't there gives E486
ref:    pattern.txt *E486*
quote:  When no match is found you get the error: *E486* Pattern not found
given:  o|ne two
keys:   /zzz<CR>
expect: o|ne two
msg:    E486: Pattern not found: zzz

=== n with no match gives E486 and stays put
ref:    pattern.txt *E486*
quote:  When no match is found you get the error: *E486* Pattern not found
given:  o|ne two
keys:   /zzz<CR>0n
expect: |one two
msg:    E486: Pattern not found: zzz

=== search lands on a multibyte line at the byte column
ref:    pattern.txt *pattern-multibyte*
quote:  Patterns will also work with multibyte characters, mostly as you would expect.
given:  |é漢字 foo
keys:   /foo<CR>
expect: é漢字 |foo

=== search for a multibyte character
ref:    pattern.txt *pattern-multibyte*
quote:  Patterns will also work with multibyte characters, mostly as you would expect.
given:  |abc 漢字 字
keys:   /字<CR>n
expect: abc 漢字 |字
